  "result": "Shell completion now handles `#` correctly: an argument like `a#b` is no longer cut short, and `#x` no longer drops everything after it.\n\n**Fix:** I added `lex.commenters = \"\"` to `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py`. The splitter was treating `#` as the start of a comment. Bash, Zsh, Fish and PowerShell completion all use this function, so the fix covers all four.\n\n**Tests:** I added two cases to `test_split_arg_string` in `tests/test_parser.py`:\n- `cli a#b c` \u2192 `[\"cli\", \"a#b\", \"c\"]`\n- `cli #x y` \u2192 `[\"cli\", \"#x\", \"y\"]`\n\nBoth new cases fail without the fix. With it, the parser, shell-completion and deprecation test files all pass (95 tests). I skipped the optional end-to-end case in `test_full_complete`.\n\n**Changelog:** `CHANGES.md` only had a released 8.5.0 section, so I added a new \"Version 8.5.1, Unreleased\" section with an entry for this fix.\n\nNothing is committed.",
